agility of them like i  say made us feel like there was a better  way to engage the public in this subject  and then just merely documenting what's  what's been going on so then we go to  the next level of our our project so  we're also going to 3d model those five  objects that we've told the ancient and  modern stories of and make those 3d  models available online so  people can download them themselves and  host their own pop-up exhibitions around  the world or simply print one off for  their mum for Christmas I don't know  whether you know now but but you can  actually print porcelain and with a  glaze on it as well that's very specific  and I don't know quite how it works  because I'm not doing that part of the  project but it looks much more real than  you imagine and you can also print it  very crudely which has its own artistic  merits in some people's views and then  the third level of our story is on this  website we're going to encourage people  to upload their own stories and their  own objects now it might be something  which has a relationship with the Syrian  and Iraqi story that we're going to  start our project with and or it might  be something that has no particular  relationship to that so it may be for  instance that it's a doll and that made  its way to Kansas with a with a girl and  that becomes another object in a pop-up  exhibition or maybe somebody sitting at  home and they choose to 3d scan that  object with the three or four apps are  available on your phone for free to 3d  scan an object or just take a photo of  it tell its story and upload it onto the  site and that becomes your plunder it  could be it could be something  completely unrelated like a you know  this strange little animal are not quite  sure how to describe it a goat I guess  and which your your aunt gave you who  had some importance in your life it  could be a shopping if you were holding  an exhibition in a in a big hall of  these five objects your sixth object  could be